*.sh text eol=lf

# The Gradle wrapper. `gradlew` is a POSIX script and must keep LF endings
# even though it is checked out on Windows -- git's autocrlf would otherwise
# hand a macOS or CI machine a file its shell cannot run. Its .bat twin is the
# opposite, and the wrapper jar must never be touched at all.
mobile/android/gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary

# The self-hosted typeface. Git's own heuristic already treats it as binary,
# but saying so keeps a future autocrlf or a text-mode diff from ever touching
# a font file the browser then refuses to parse.
*.woff2 binary
